[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4559493895","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119764#issuecomment-4559493895","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119764","id":4559493895,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABD8RbBw","user":{"login":"Joy-less","id":65855333,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1ODU1MzMz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65855333?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less","html_url":"https://github.com/Joy-less","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-27T23:23:03Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T23:23:03Z","body":"This isn't surprising, because the MP3 format doesn't have seek tables.\nThis means when encoded with VBR (variable bit-rate), it has to decode the entire file up to the target offset.\nAn article about the problem: https://valor-software.com/articles/diving-into-seeking-issue-with-mp3-files\n\nI converted your MP3 to an Ogg Vorbis with FFmpeg:\n```\nffmpeg -i \"john stump - death waltz.mp3\" \"john stump - death waltz.ogg\"\n```\nAfter that, your MRP went from 14 FPS to 60(+) FPS. Ogg Vorbis uses seek tables, so it's faster.\nNote that converting from one lossy format to another will reduce the quality.\n\nFootnote:\nI also tried converting your MP3 to a CBR (constant bit-rate), which should be fast to seek (simply multiply bitrate by seek position). Sadly, the frame rate stays the same. This is probably because Godot doesn't know/check whether it's a CBR file.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4559493895/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5159521141","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119764#issuecomment-5159521141","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119764","id":5159521141,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABM4gLdQ","user":{"login":"pachuco","id":1591054,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1OTEwNTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1591054?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachuco","html_url":"https://github.com/pachuco","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachuco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachuco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachuco/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachuco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachuco/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachuco/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachuco/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachuco/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachuco/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-02T17:29:52Z","updated_at":"2026-08-02T18:49:18Z","body":"I've been pondering seeking MP3s for a different reason(reverse playback). But it will come in handy here.\nSome things I've learned:\n- mp3 frames decode to exact number of audio samples: 1152.\n- encoder gap is compensated using special frames(Xing/Info)\n- VBR and CBR+reservoir are same thing, but data is arranged differently. One can be losslessly turned into the other. This means that only difference with VBR is having to pre-walk frames and index their start offsets to have good seek. And bit reservoir is just an offset from current frame.\n- audio decoding DEPENDS on previous packets. If you try to decode two non-consecutive, you get sound soup.\n- to get coherent sound, you need to pre-decode a number of frames before decoding your actual seek frame. This number depends on how stressed the decoder is at particular point in particular mp3 frame. Can be as little as 3, as high as 9 or more.\n\nI've experimented in the name of reverse playback here: https://github.com/Polytoria/polytoria-game/issues/344#issuecomment-4472749076\n\nAnd I will attach code of my experimentation.\nOP's ache is solvable","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5159521141/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5159648602","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119764#issuecomment-5159648602","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119764","id":5159648602,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABM4n9Wg","user":{"login":"pachuco","id":1591054,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1OTEwNTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1591054?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachuco","html_url":"https://github.com/pachuco","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachuco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachuco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachuco/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachuco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachuco/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachuco/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachuco/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachuco/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachuco/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-02T18:03:27Z","updated_at":"2026-08-02T18:09:10Z","body":"https://gist.github.com/pachuco/8894f431f0048a9d63d10e46722687d9\nReverse playback experiment, which is pathological application of seeking(stress test).\n\nAlternative I can think of is low-priority pre-computing seek tables for each mp3 sound asset on load.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5159648602/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5546929641","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119764#issuecomment-5546929641","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119764","id":5546929641,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSp9t6Q","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-04T22:00:11Z","updated_at":"2026-09-06T03:11:08Z","body":"Regression from #96547. The issue is, in part, `dr_mp3`'s fault.\n\nWhile `minimp3` handled seek tables automatically, it's an optional feature in `dr_mp3`, which expects that to be done manually.\n\nI've submitted a PR that does exactly that.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5546929641/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]